---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { disclaimer, fullCredits } from '../data/legal';
import { siteName } from '../data/site';
import { getPublishedWeeks } from '../lib/posts';

await getPublishedWeeks();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How this site grades a pick record, credits its sources, and states its limits."
>
  <p class="kicker">How the ledger is kept</p>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <div class="prose">
  <p>
    {siteName} publishes matchup notes and a public pick record. The rules on this page are the whole
    standard.
  </p>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  {fullCredits.map((line) => <p>{line}</p>)}

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>{disclaimer}</p>

  <h2>Closing line</h2>
  <p>
    The closing line is the lower-middle line of N US books in the last valid pre-kick snapshot. Sort
    the books' lines ascending and take element floor((n-1)/2). That is a real book line, never an
    average.
  </p>
  <p>
    That snapshot is the last one stored before kickoff, typically 5 to 75 minutes before kickoff. It
    is not the true close at kickoff.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Three or more books: that lower-middle line. Source: odds_api.</li>
    <li>Thin: 1-2 books. The same lower-middle line of those books is used. Source: odds_api_thin.</li>
    <li>Stale: the snapshot is more than 180 minutes before kickoff. Source: odds_api_stale.</li>
    <li>nflverse: no books, so the nflverse line is used. Source: nflverse.</li>
    <li>Ungraded: no line from either source. The site does not guess.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Lines are shown as the lower-middle line of N US books. Book names are not shown, and there are
    no book links.
  </p>

  <h2 id="grading">Grading</h2>
  <p>
    Each pick is a flat 1 unit. Grading assumes standard −110 odds. A win is +0.909 units, a loss is
    −1.000 units, and a push is 0 units. Win percentage excludes pushes. CLV is shown for reference
    only and does not change the grade. Results are in units, never dollars.
  </p>

  <h2>Lock rule</h2>
  <p>
    A pick is rejected when picked_at is at or after kickoff, or when the server push time is at or
    after kickoff. Rejected picks are marked rejected – late and left out of the record. A client-set
    commit time does not lock a pick.
  </p>

  <h2>Film</h2>
  <p>
    Film is link-out only. This site does not rehost, download, or frame film. There is no fantasy
    content.
  </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
